return {h=65,w=2350,cr=45,hc=5,bh=70,gr="slow",eg={"water2","dragon"},st={95,125,79,60,100,81},ab={{22,0},{153,1}},genus={en="Atrocious Pokémon",es="Pokémon Atrocidad",pt="Pokémon Atroz"},flavor={en={[1]="Rarely seen in the wild. Huge and vicious, it is capable of destroying entire cities in a rage.",[2]="Rarely seen in the wild. Huge and vicious, it is capable of destroying entire cities in a rage.",[3]="Brutally vicious and enormously destructive. Known for totally destroying cities in ancient times.",[4]="They say that during past wars, GYARADOS would appear and leave blazing ruins in its wake.",[5]="Once it appears, it goes on a rampage. It remains enraged until it demolishes everything around it.",[6]="It appears whenever there is world conflict, burning down any place it travels through.",[7]="When MAGIKARP evolves into GYARADOS, its brain cells undergo a structural transformation. It is said that this transformation is to blame for this Pokémon’s wildly violent nature.",[8]="Once GYARADOS goes on a rampage, its ferociously violent blood doesn’t calm until it has burned everything down. There are records of this Pokémon’s rampages lasting a whole month.",[9]="It is an extremely vicious and violent Pokémon. When humans begin to fight, it will appear and burn everything to the ground with intensely hot flames.",[10]="It has an extremely aggressive nature. The HYPER BEAM it shoots from its mouth totally incinerates all targets.",[11]="Rarely seen in the wild. Huge and vicious, it is capable of destroying entire cities in a rage.",[12]="Once it appears, its rage never settles until it has razed the fields and mountains around it.",[13]="In ancient literature, there is a record of a GYARADOS that razed a village when violence flared.",[14]="Once it begins to rampage, a GYARADOS will burn everything down, even in a harsh storm.",[15]="They say that during past strife, GYARADOS would appear and leave blazing ruins in its wake.",[16]="Once it appears, it goes on a rampage. It remains enraged until it demolishes everything around it.",[17]="Once it begins to rampage, a Gyarados will burn everything down, even in a harsh storm.",[18]="Once it begins to rampage, a Gyarados will burn everything down, even in a harsh storm.",[21]="Once it begins to rampage, a Gyarados will burn everything down, even in a harsh storm.",[22]="Once it begins to rampage, a Gyarados will burn everything down, even in a harsh storm.",[23]="In ancient literature, there is a record of a Gyarados that razed a village when violence flared.",[24]="Rarely seen in the wild. Huge and vicious, it is capable of destroying entire cities in a rage.",[25]="When Magikarp evolves into Gyarados, its brain cells undergo a structural transformation. It is said that this transformation is to blame for this Pokémon’s wildly violent nature.",[26]="Once Gyarados goes on a rampage, its ferociously violent blood doesn’t calm until it has burned everything down. There are records of this Pokémon’s rampages lasting a whole month.",[27]="A tale is told of a town that angered Gyarados. Before the sun rose the next day, flames utterly consumed the town, leaving not a trace behind.",[28]="There are people who swear that any place Gyarados appears is fated for destruction.",[29]="It fires hyper beams in all directions, burning the surrounding area to ash. There are some regions where it’s called “the deity of destruction.”",[30]="The energy from evolution stimulated its brain cells strongly, causing it to become very ferocious.",[31]="Brutally vicious and enormously destructive. Known for totally destroying cities in ancient times.",[32]="Brutally vicious and enormously destructive. Known for totally destroying cities in ancient times.",[33]="It has an extremely aggressive nature. The Hyper Beam it shoots from its mouth totally incinerates all targets.",[34]="Once it begins to rampage, a Gyarados will burn everything down, even in a harsh storm.",[39]="I suspect this Pokémon to be the true identity of a dragon written of in ancient texts, which claimed that it razed an entire village with white-hot beams from its maw."},es={[23]="En la literatura antigua se dice que un Gyarados rebosante de violencia arrasó un poblado.",[24]="No es frecuente verlo en su medio. Es enorme y malvado, y capaz de destruir ciudades enteras de un ataque.",[25]="Cuando Magikarp evoluciona y se convierte en Gyarados, sufre un cambio estructural en las células del cerebro. Dicen que esa transformación es la causa de la naturaleza violenta y salvaje de este Pokémon.",[26]="Una vez que Gyarados se desmanda, la presión incontrolable y enrabiada de la sangre no se le calmará hasta que no haya quemado todo lo que le rodea. Según parece, a este Pokémon le duran los arranques de cólera hasta un mes.",[27]="Cuentan que un Gyarados se enfadó tanto que arrasó un poblado en una sola noche y no dejó ni rastro.",[28]="Alguna gente cree que aquellos lugares donde aparece Gyarados están abocados a la destrucción.",[29]="Allí donde alcanza su Hiperrayo la tierra queda carbonizada por completo. En algunas regiones lo consideran una deidad destructiva.",[30]="La energía desprendida durante la evolución afecta de forma irreversible sus neuronas, dando origen a su agresividad manifiesta.",[31]="Este Pokémon tan salvaje como destructivo es conocido por haber reducido a escombros ciudades enteras en el pasado.",[32]="Este Pokémon tan salvaje como destructivo es conocido por haber reducido a escombros ciudades enteras en el pasado.",[33]="Es exageradamente agresivo. El Hiperrayo que lanza por la boca reduce a cenizas todo lo que encuentra.",[34]="Cuando monta en cólera, puede quemarlo todo, incluso en medio de la más violenta tormenta."},pt="Suspeito que este Pokémon seja a verdadeira identidade de um dragão descrito em textos antigos, que dizem que ele arrasou uma vila inteira com raios incandescentes saídos da boca."},evo={{s=129},{s=130,from=129,c={{t="level-up",lv=20}}}},moves={[1]={1,44,1,82